/E (To justify their presence in Zimbabwe protagonists of proselytisation and colonization posed as harbingers of culture and civilization to Africa impelled by a humanitarian impulse. For this interpretation to succeed, the existence of indigenous education had to be denied. Consequently, a number of myths relating to indigenous education had to be fabricated in support of the theory of benevolence. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
